    {
      "id": 78,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Relevance-floor candidate drops (#394)",
      "description": "Candidates dropped because their (boosted) cross-encoder score fell below RERANK_SCORE_FLOOR. The per-query series is the tuning signal after a reranker model change (raw logit scales differ per model, per the #415 caveat in .env.example/values.yaml): a jump means the floor is now cutting into normal traffic; sustained zero with a floor set means it does nothing. Queries emptied entirely by the floor surface separately as outcome=\"empty\" in the throughput panel.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 30
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "prometheus"
